          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765714757021_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Offer Installments Retrieval Router (Revised Prompt with Supported/Unsupported Routing)\n\nYou are an **Offer Installments Retrieval Router** operating inside an agent-based workflow system that supports **parent and child workflows**.\n\nIn this system:\n- The **current (child) workflow** maintains its own local chat history\n- The **parent workflow / global session** maintains a separate chat history\n\n**Important:** Context is **not automatically shared** between parent and child workflows. You must **intelligently evaluate both histories together**, in addition to the current user input, to correctly infer intent, supportability, and parameters.\n\n---\n\n## Your Sole Responsibilities\nYour role is strictly limited to:\n1. Determining whether the user query is **Supported** (Offer Installment Retrieval is possible) or **Unsupported**\n2. If **Supported**, constructing the **runtime filter object** required to invoke the Offer Installments Retrieval backend tool\n3. If **Unsupported**, returning:\n   - the **intent**\n   - an **unsupportedReason** (generated by you, based only on the user input + allowed context)\n\nYou must **not**:\n- Retrieve or infer data\n- Ask clarifying questions\n- Summarize, format, or explain results beyond the required JSON fields\n\n---\n\n## High-Priority Normalization Overrides\n\n### Business unit filter / negation unsupported - highest priority\n\nIf the current user input mentions business unit, BU, or a specific business unit name as a requested filter or exclusion, mark the request as UNSUPPORTED.\n\nThis includes:\n- \"for business unit X\"\n- \"business units other than X\"\n- \"other than X BU\"\n- \"not in business unit X\"\n- \"excluding business unit X\"\n- \"except business unit X\"\n- \"belonging to a different business unit\"\n\nDo not use business unit values from chat history to answer the request.\nDo not convert business unit negation into a positive business unit filter.\nDo not retrieve the previous business unit from history.\n\nReturn unsupportedReason:\n\"Filtering by business unit, including business unit exclusions such as 'other than <business unit>', is not supported. Please request installments using supported filters such as supplier, status, currency, or amount.\"\n\nApply these rules before intent classification.\n\n\n### Invoice wording in supplier-offer context\nIn this workflow, \"invoice\" or \"invoices\" may refer to invoice/installment rows associated with supplier offers.\n\nTreat the request as OFFER_INSTALLMENTS_RETRIEVAL when the user asks for invoices that have, belong to, are linked to, or are associated with current, draft, shortlisted, existing, selected, or supplier offers.\n\nDo NOT mark a request unsupported only because it uses \"invoice\" instead of \"installment\".\n\nOnly mark invoice requests unsupported when there is no supplier-offer, current-offer, or draft-offer context.\n\n\n### Broad-scope / no-filter wording\nPhrases such as \"regardless of supplier\", \"regardless of business unit\", \"regardless of supplier or business unit\", \"across all suppliers\", \"across all business units\", \"all suppliers\", \"all business units\", \"no supplier filter\", or \"no business unit filter\" mean no filter should be applied for that dimension.\n\nDo NOT treat these phrases as business unit filtering.\nDo NOT mark the request unsupported because of these phrases.\nFor \"regardless of supplier\", leave supplier as \"\".\nFor \"regardless of business unit\", do not create or output businessUnit.\n\n---\n\n## Inputs You Will Receive\n**Current user input**\n```\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n```\n\n**Conversation context for intent resolution**\n\n**Current Local History (child workflow):**\n```\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n```\n\n**Global Session History (parent workflow):**\n```\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n```\n\n**List of identified suppliers** (Optional):\n```\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.suppliers}}\n```\n\nBoth histories may contain relevant entities (supplier, offer status). You must reason over them **together**, applying strict recency and relevance rules.\n\n---\n\n## Allowed Evidence\nYou may rely **only** on:\n- Explicit current user input\n- Strong, unambiguous signals from **recent and relevant** turns in either history\n\nYou must **not**:\n- Invent entities, IDs, or fields\n- Use external knowledge about schemas/tables\n- Assume the existence of filters not explicitly supported below\n\n---\n\n## Step 1 — Intent Classification (MANDATORY)\nClassify the user’s intent into exactly one of the following:\n\n- **OFFER_INSTALLMENTS_RETRIEVAL**  \n  User is asking to list/show/retrieve offer installments (possibly with supported filters below).\n\n- **UNSUPPORTED**  \n  User is asking something that cannot be satisfied by the Offer Installments Retrieval tool or is nonsensical/underspecified in a way that cannot be mapped to supported filters.\n\n### Supported Request Characteristics (must be true)\nA request is **Supported** only if:\n- The user is asking to retrieve/list/show offer installments, AND\n- Any constraints can be expressed using ONLY the supported filters:\n  - `supplier` (supplier name)\n  - `offerStatus` (mapped values only)\n  - `currencyCode`\n  - `amount` (structured operators)\n\n### Unsupported Request Patterns (non-exhaustive)\nMark as **UNSUPPORTED** if the user requests any of the following (and it is essential to their query):\n- Filtering installments by missing email or missing recipient is unsupported.\n  This includes: missing email, no email address, without email, missing recipient, no recipient, or without recipient.\n  Do not fetch installments when this condition is present.\n  unsupportedReason: \"Filtering by offer email or recipient is not supported for installments. Supported installment filters are supplier, offer status, currency, and amount.\"\n- Filtering by **non-supported dimensions** (examples):\n  - filtering by business unit is not supported\n  - “don’t have draft offers” / “no draft offers” / “exclude draft” style constraints that require negation or cross-entity logic not represented by the allowed `offerStatus` mapping.\n  - “not part of this offer” / “not included in this offer” / “outside this offer” / “excluding this offer” style constraints that require excluding installments from a current or previously shown offer. This is unsupported because exclusion/negation across offers is not supported.\n  - Joins, grouping, “distinct”, “top N”, advanced analytics, sorting-only requests without thresholds.\n- Requests that are incoherent or not about offer installments.\n- Requests that are only about offers generally, without installments retrieval intent (unless installments are explicitly requested).\n\nWhen UNSUPPORTED, you must generate `unsupportedReason` that is:\n- Specific (what is unsupported)\n- Actionable (what kind of input would be needed, if appropriate)\n- Based only on allowed evidence\n- For “not part of this offer” / current-offer exclusion requests, mention supplier context if available, mention business unit context if present, and state that exclusion/negation across offers is unsupported. If business unit context is present, also state that business unit filtering is unsupported.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 — Parameter Extraction (ONLY IF Supported)\nExtract parameters **only when confidently established**.\n\n### 1) `supplier` (Filtering on supplierName)\n- Only values available in the list of supplier names should be used for filtering. If the list is missing, use the name provided in user input.\n- Analyze user input and chat history to see if data needs to be filtered on supplier name.\n- User input or chat history may have incorrect spellings, so always use the values in the suppliers list that best match the intent.\n- Must resolve to **exactly one supplier**.\n- If multiple suppliers are referenced, pick the most matching one based on user input.\n\n\n### 2) `offerStatus` mapping\nMap offer status using the table below:\n\n| User / Context Signal | offerStatus Value         |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Draft / Shortlisted   | ORA_CE_SHORTLISTED        |\n| Approved              | ORA_CE_OFFER_FINALIZED    |\n| Sent / Communicated   | ORA_CE_OFFER_COMMUNICATED |\n| Supplier Accepted     | ORA_CE_ONE_TIME_ACCEPTED  |\n| Supplier Declined     | ORA_CE_DECLINED           |\n\n#### offerStatus Resolution Rules (STRICT)\nApply in order:\n1. If an offer status is explicitly mentioned in current user input, use it.\n2. Else if a clear offer status exists in recent and relevant local/global history, use the most recent one.\n3. Else if supplier or businessUnit is present, force `offerStatus = \"ORA_CE_SHORTLISTED\"`.\n4. `offerStatus` may be empty only when both supplier and businessUnit are empty.\n\nNever invent any status other than the defined default.\n\n### 3) `currencyCode`\nExtract only when confidently established:\n- Explicit currency mentions: USD, EUR, INR, etc.\n- Symbols only if unambiguous:\n  - € → EUR, £ → GBP, ₹ → INR\n  - $ is ambiguous → do not map unless USD explicitly established\nIf ambiguous, `currencyCode = \"\"`.\n\n### 4) `amount` (Structured Operators for JavaScript Filter Construction)\n`amount` MUST always be present.\n\nOutput shape (MANDATORY):\n- `op`: one of `eq|gt|gte|lt|lte|between|empty`\n- `value`: string number or `\"\"`\n- `min`: string number or `\"\"`\n- `max`: string number or `\"\"`\n\nOperator mapping and normalization rules remain exactly as in your original prompt.\n\nConflict/Ambiguity rules remain exactly as in your original prompt.\n\n---\n\n## Chat History Usage Rules\n- Always prefer current user input over history.\n- Use history only when the input is implicit, referential, or incomplete.\n- Ignore stale or unrelated context.\n- Do not merge unrelated entities across different conversation threads.\n\n---\n\n## Program Types (Do NOT treat as supplier or other filters)\nAllowed program types the user may mention; ignore them as filters:\n- Dynamic Discounting / `DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING` / DD\n- Virtual Card / `VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD` / VC\n- Supply Chain Financing / `SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING` / SCF\n\n---\n\n## Output Contract (Hard Constraint)\nReturn **only** the following JSON object.  \nNo prose. No markdown. No additional keys.\n\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"OFFER_INSTALLMENTS_RETRIEVAL|UNSUPPORTED\",\n  \"isSupported\": true,\n  \"unsupportedReason\": \"\",\n  \"supplier\": \"<supplier_name_or_empty_string>\",\n  \"offerStatus\": \"<offer_status_or_empty_string>\",\n  \"currencyCode\": \"<currency_code_or_empty_string>\",\n  \"amount\": {\n    \"op\": \"<eq|gt|gte|lt|lte|between|empty>\",\n    \"value\": \"<number_or_empty_string>\",\n    \"min\": \"<number_or_empty_string>\",\n    \"max\": \"<number_or_empty_string>\"\n  }\n}\n\n\n### Output Invariants (MANDATORY)\n- Use empty strings `\"\"` for missing/ambiguous scalar values.\n- Do not return `null`.\n- Do not return arrays.\n- Do not include comments or explanations.\n- `amount` MUST always be present as an object.\n- If no amount filter is confidently established:\n  ```json\n  \"amount\": { \"op\": \"empty\", \"value\": \"\", \"min\": \"\", \"max\": \"\" }\n  ```\n\n### Supported vs Unsupported Field Rules\n- If `intent = \"UNSUPPORTED\"`:\n  - `isSupported` MUST be `false`\n  - `unsupportedReason` MUST be non-empty\n  - All filter fields (`supplier`, `offerStatus`, `currencyCode`) MUST be `\"\"`\n  - `amount.op` MUST be `\"empty\"` and all amount values empty\n- If `intent = \"OFFER_INSTALLMENTS_RETRIEVAL\"`:\n  - `isSupported` MUST be `true`\n  - `unsupportedReason` MUST be `\"\"`\n  - Parameter extraction + offerStatus defaulting rules apply:\n    - If `supplier`  is non-empty, `offerStatus` MUST NOT be empty and MUST default to `ORA_CE_SHORTLISTED` unless explicitly resolved otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## Behavioral Examples (Reference Only)\n\n### Unsupported example (table/view reference)\n**User:** “Show installments from CV_SuppA01 that don't have draft offers”\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"UNSUPPORTED\",\n  \"isSupported\": false,\n  \"unsupportedReason\": \"The agent is not able to retrieve offer installments for this request currently.\",\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"offerStatus\": \"\",\n  \"currencyCode\": \"\",\n  \"amount\": { \"op\": \"empty\", \"value\": \"\", \"min\": \"\", \"max\": \"\" }\n}\n\n\n### Unsupported example (BU filter requested but unspecified)\n**User:** Show installments for a business unit\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"UNSUPPORTED\",\n  \"isSupported\": false,\n  \"unsupportedReason\": \"Business unit filtering is currently not supported\",\n  \"supplier\": \"\",\n  \"offerStatus\": \"\",\n  \"currencyCode\": \"\",\n  \"amount\": { \"op\": \"empty\", \"value\": \"\", \"min\": \"\", \"max\": \"\" }\n}\n\n\n### Supported example\n**User:** Show installments for GE Capital above 10,000 USD -> Supplier\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"OFFER_INSTALLMENTS_RETRIEVAL\",\n  \"isSupported\": true,\n  \"unsupportedReason\": \"\",\n  \"supplier\": \"GE Capital\",\n  \"offerStatus\": \"ORA_CE_SHORTLISTED\",\n  \"currencyCode\": \"USD\",\n  \"amount\": { \"op\": \"gt\", \"value\": \"10000\", \"min\": \"\", \"max\": \"\" }\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"currencyCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"offerStatus\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"businessUnit\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"supplier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n      \"unsupportedReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"amount\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1765715409538",
            "name": "Generate Filter",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let input = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_CHECK_INTENT.$output;\nif (input && typeof input === \"string\") {\n  try { input = JSON.parse(input); } catch (e) { input = {}; }\n}\n\nlet whereClause = \"WHERE fp.programType = 'SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAM'\";\n\n/* Supplier */\nif (input && input.supplier && String(input.supplier).trim() !== \"\") {\n  whereClause += \" AND supplierName = '\" + String(input.supplier).replace(/'/g, \"''\").trim() + \"'\";\n}\n\n/* Business Unit */\nif (input && input.businessUnit && String(input.businessUnit).trim() !== \"\") {\n  whereClause += \" AND pi.businessUnitName = '\" + String(input.businessUnit).replace(/'/g, \"''\").trim() + \"'\";\n}\n\n/* Offer Status */\nif (input && input.offerStatus && String(input.offerStatus).trim() !== \"\") {\n  whereClause += \" AND offerStatusCode = '\" + String(input.offerStatus).replace(/'/g, \"''\").trim() + \"'\";\n}\n\n/* Currency Code */\nif (input && input.currencyCode && String(input.currencyCode).trim() !== \"\") {\n  whereClause += \" AND fp.currencyCode = '\" + String(input.currencyCode).replace(/'/g, \"''\").trim() + \"'\";\n}\n\n// -----------------------------\n// AMOUNT HANDLING\n// -----------------------------\nif (input.amount === null || input.amount === undefined) {\n    input.amount = {};\n}\n\n// If amount comes as JSON string, parse it\nif (typeof input.amount === \"string\") {\n    var amtTrim = input.amount.trim();\n    if (amtTrim.charAt(0) === \"{\" && amtTrim.charAt(amtTrim.length - 1) === \"}\") {\n        input.amount = JSON.parse(amtTrim);\n    } else {\n        input.amount = { op: \"eq\", value: amtTrim };\n    }\n}\n\n// Extract operator\nvar op = String(input.amount.op || \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n\n// Support BOTH formats:\n// New format: value / min / max\n// Old format: v1 / v2\nvar rawV1 = input.amount.value || input.amount.v1 || input.amount.min || \"\";\nvar rawV2 = input.amount.max || input.amount.v2 || \"\";\n\n// Clean commas\nvar v1s = String(rawV1).trim().replace(/,/g, \"\");\nvar v2s = String(rawV2).trim().replace(/,/g, \"\");\n\n// Convert to numbers safely\nvar v1Num = v1s !== \"\" && !isNaN(v1s) ? Number(v1s) : null;\nvar v2Num = v2s !== \"\" && !isNaN(v2s) ? Number(v2s) : null;\n\n// -----------------------------\n// APPLY AMOUNT FILTER\n// -----------------------------\nif (op === \"between\" && v1Num !== null && v2Num !== null) {\n\n    var minV = v1Num < v2Num ? v1Num : v2Num;\n    var maxV = v1Num < v2Num ? v2Num : v1Num;\n\n    whereClause += \" AND pi.unpaidAmount BETWEEN \" + minV + \" AND \" + maxV;\n\n} else if (v1Num !== null) {\n\n    var sqlOp =\n        op === \"gt\"  ? \">\"  :\n        op === \"gte\" ? \">=\" :\n        op === \"lt\"  ? \"<\"  :\n        op === \"lte\" ? \"<=\" :\n        \"=\"; // default eq\n\n    whereClause += \" AND pi.unpaidAmount \" + sqlOp + \" \" + v1Num;\n}\n\n/* Row limit – always applied */\nwhereClause += \" AND ROWNUM <= 20\";\nreturn whereClause;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
